window.onload = loadStylesheet;
```

In the solution, the `loadStylesheet` function creates a new `link` element and sets its `rel` attribute to "stylesheet". It then uses `window.matchMedia` to check the maximum width of the viewport. If the maximum width is 768 pixels or less, it sets the `href` attribute of the `link` element to the mobile stylesheet URL; otherwise, it sets it to the desktop stylesheet URL. Finally, the function appends the `link` element to the `head` of the HTML document. The `loadStylesheet` function is called when the page loads to dynamically load the appropriate stylesheet based on the user's device type.

