   a. If `i` is equal to `x`, skip to the next iteration.
   b. If `a[i]` is greater than `a[x]`, set `val[x][a[i]]` to 1 and increment `at`.
   c. If `a[i]` is less than `a[x]`, set `val[x][a[i]]` to -1 and decrement `at`.
   d. If `a[i]` is equal to `a[x]`, add `i` to the `parent[x]` vector.
3. Set `ans[at]` to the size of the `parent[x]` vector.

Your task is to complete the `calculateAnswer` function and return the `ans` array after performing the above steps for the given input `x`.

