    std::string word = "this";

    int occurrences = countWordOccurrences(text, word);
    std::cout << "Number of occurrences of the word '" << word << "': " << occurrences << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

The `countWordOccurrences` function first converts both the input `text` and `word` to lowercase using `std::transform` and `::tolower` for case-insensitive matching. It then uses a while loop to find and count the occurrences of the word in the text using `std::string::find`. The function returns the count of occurrences. The main function demonstrates the usage of the `countWordOccurrences` function with a sample text and word, printing the number of occurrences to the console.

