### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a function that checks whether a given HTML document is well-formed. For the purpose of this problem, a well-formed HTML document should adhere to the following rules:
1. The document must start with the `<!DOCTYPE html>` declaration.
2. The opening and closing tags must be properly nested and balanced.
3. All tags must be properly closed, either with a closing tag or a self-closing tag.
4. Any attribute values must be enclosed in quotes.

You need to implement a function `isWellFormedHTML(html)` that takes a string `html` representing an HTML document and returns `true` if the document is well-formed according to the rules above, and `false` otherwise.

Example:
```javascript
isWellFormedHTML('<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>Sample</title></head><body><h1>Hello, World!</h1></body></html>'); // true
isWellFormedHTML('<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><title>Sample</title></head><body><h1>Hello, World!</h1>'); // false (unclosed <body> tag)
```

### Solution:
```javascript
function isWellFormedHTML(html) {
  const stack = [];
  const tagRegex = /<\s*\/?\s*([a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9]*)\s*.*?>/g;
  let match;
  while ((match = tagRegex.exec(html)) !== null) {
    const tag = match[1];
    if (tag.startsWith('/')) {
      if (stack.length === 0 || stack.pop() !== tag.substring(1)) {
        return false; // Closing tag mismatch
      }
    } else if (!tag.endsWith('/')) {
      stack.push(tag);
    }
  }
  return stack.length === 0;
}
```

