    // Your implementation here
}
```

The function should take an integer array `inputArray` and return an integer array where each element represents the count of set bits in the binary representation of the corresponding element in the input array.

For example, if the input array is `[5, 3, 9]`, the output array should be `[2, 2, 2]` because the binary representations of `5`, `3`, and `9` are `101`, `011`, and `1001` respectively, and they each contain 2 set bits.

### Solution:
```java
public int[] countSetBits(int[] inputArray) {
    int[] bitCountArray = new int[inputArray.length];
    for (int i = 0; i < inputArray.length; i++) {
        int num = inputArray[i];
        int count = 0;
        while (num > 0) {
            count += num & 1;
            num >>= 1;
        }
        bitCountArray[i] = count;
    }
    return bitCountArray;
}
```

