### Problem:
You are given a C++ code snippet that contains a preprocessor directive `#endif`. Your task is to write a program that can identify and count the occurrences of this directive in a given C++ source file.

Write a C++ program that takes a filename as input and outputs the number of occurrences of the `#endif` directive in the file. The program should consider the possibility of the directive being present on the same line as other code or with trailing whitespace.

For example, given the following C++ source file `example.cpp`:
```cpp
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    // Some code
    #endif
    #endif // End of file
    return 0;
}
```
The program should output:
```
2
```

Assume that the input file will be a valid C++ source file and that the `#endif` directive will only appear in the context of preprocessor directives.

### Solution:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <string>

int countEndifDirectives(const std::string& filename) {
    std::ifstream file(filename);
    if (!file.is_open()) {
        std::cerr << "Error opening file" << std::endl;
        return -1;
    }

    std::string line;
    int count = 0;
    while (std::getline(file, line)) {
        size_t pos = line.find("#endif");
        while (pos != std::string::npos) {
            if (pos == 0 || line[pos - 1] == ' ' || line[pos - 1] == '\t') {
                count++;
            }
            pos = line.find("#endif", pos + 1);
        }
    }

    file.close();
    return count;
}

int main() {
    std::string filename = "example.cpp";  // Replace with the actual filename
    int occurrences = countEndifDirectives(filename);
    if (occurrences >= 0) {
        std::cout << occurrences << std::endl;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

