### Problem:
You are tasked with implementing a circular buffer data structure in Rust. A circular buffer is a fixed-size buffer that overwrites old data when the buffer is full. It has a read pointer and a write pointer, and it supports operations for reading from and writing to the buffer. The buffer should be implemented as a generic type that can store any type of data. Your task is to implement the `CircularBuffer` struct with the following methods:
- `new(size: usize) -> CircularBuffer`: Creates a new circular buffer with the specified size.
- `write(&mut self, data: T) -> Result<(), &str>`: Writes data to the buffer. If the buffer is full, it should overwrite the oldest data and return an error message "Buffer full".
- `read(&mut self) -> Option<T>`: Reads data from the buffer. If the buffer is empty, it should return `None`.

You should also implement the `IntoIterator` trait for the `CircularBuffer` struct, allowing iteration over the elements in the buffer.

Your implementation should be able to handle any type `T` that implements the `Copy` trait.

```rust
struct CircularBuffer<T: Copy> {
    buffer: Vec<Option<T>>,
    read_index: usize,
    write_index: usize,
}

impl<T: Copy> CircularBuffer<T> {
    fn new(size: usize) -> CircularBuffer<T> {
        CircularBuffer {
            buffer: vec![None; size],
            read_index: 0,
            write_index: 0,
        }
    }

    fn write(&mut self, data: T) -> Result<(), &str> {
        if self.buffer[self.write_index].is_some() {
            self.read_index = (self.read_index + 1) % self.buffer.len();
        }
        self.buffer[self.write_index] = Some(data);
        self.write_index = (self.write_index + 1) % self.buffer.len();
        Ok(())
    }

    fn read(&mut self) -> Option<T> {
        if let Some(data) = self.buffer[self.read_index] {
            self.buffer[self.read_index] = None;
            self.read_index = (self.read_index + 1) % self.buffer.len();
            Some(data)
        } else {
            None
        }
    }
}

impl<T: Copy> IntoIterator for CircularBuffer<T> {
    type Item = T;
    type IntoIter = CircularBufferIterator<T>;

    fn into_iter(self) -> Self::IntoIter {
        CircularBufferIterator {
            buffer: self,
            index: 0,
        }
    }
}

struct CircularBufferIterator<T: Copy> {
    buffer: CircularBuffer<T>,
    index: usize,
}

impl<T: Copy> Iterator for CircularBufferIterator<T> {
    type Item = T;

    fn next(&mut self) -> Option<Self::Item> {
        if self.index < self.buffer.buffer.len() {
            let data = self.buffer.buffer[self.index];
            self.index += 1;
            data
        } else {
            None
        }
    }
}
```

