You are tasked with implementing a simple collision detection system for a 2D game. The game world consists of various entities, each with a rectangular bounding box representing its position and size. Your goal is to write a function that determines whether two entities are colliding with each other based on their bounding boxes.

You are given the following struct definition for an entity:

```cpp
struct Entity {
    int x; // x-coordinate of the top-left corner
    int y; // y-coordinate of the top-left corner
    int width; // width of the bounding box
    int height; // height of the bounding box
};
```

You need to implement the following function:

```cpp
