You are tasked with implementing a pagination algorithm for a web application. The application is written in PHP and uses the Yii framework. The provided code snippet is a part of the pagination feature and includes the rendering of the pagination controls.

Your task is to write a function that takes in the total number of items, the current page, and the items per page, and generates the necessary HTML for the pagination controls. The pagination controls should include links for navigating to the previous and next pages, as well as direct links to specific pages. The function should also handle the case when there are a large number of pages, providing a way to navigate to different sections of the paginated data.

You should implement the pagination algorithm in PHP, ensuring that the generated HTML is compatible with the Yii framework and adheres to the styling and structure used in the provided code snippet.

Write a function with the following signature:
```php
function generatePaginationHTML($totalItems, $currentPage, $itemsPerPage) {
    // Your implementation here
}
```

### Solution:
```php
function generatePaginationHTML($totalItems, $currentPage, $itemsPerPage) {
    $totalPages = ceil($totalItems / $itemsPerPage);
    $html = '<div id="pagination">';

    // Previous page link
    if ($currentPage > 1) {
        $html .= '<a href="?page=' . ($currentPage - 1) . '">Previous</a>';
    }

    // Page links
    for ($i = 1; $i <= $totalPages; $i++) {
        if ($i == $currentPage) {
            $html .= '<span>' . $i . '</span>';
        } else {
            $html .= '<a href="?page=' . $i . '">' . $i . '</a>';
        }
    }

    // Next page link
    if ($currentPage < $totalPages) {
        $html .= '<a href="?page=' . ($currentPage + 1) . '">Next</a>';
    }

    $html .= '</div>';

    return $html;
}
```

This solution calculates the total number of pages based on the total items and items per page. It then generates HTML for the pagination controls, including links for previous and next pages, as well as direct links to specific pages. The function ensures that the generated HTML is compatible with the Yii framework and can be used to navigate through the paginated data.

