You are working on a web application that utilizes a popular CSS-in-JS library called styled-components. The code snippet provided is a part of the styled-components usage in the application. Your task is to write a function that parses the given styled-components code and extracts the CSS properties and their values for each styled component.

You need to implement a function `parseStyledComponents` that takes the styled-components code as a string input and returns an object containing the component names and their respective CSS properties and values.

The input styled-components code will consist of multiple styled components, each defined using the `styled` function from the styled-components library. Each styled component will have a unique name and may contain one or more CSS properties and their values.

The function should return an object in the following format:
```javascript
{
  componentName1: {
    property1: value1,
    property2: value2,
    // ... other properties and values
  },
  componentName2: {
    property1: value1,
    property2: value2,
    // ... other properties and values
  },
  // ... other components and their properties
}
```

For example, given the input styled-components code:
```javascript
const FirstChar = styled.span.attrs({ singleCharacter: true })`
  z-index: 1;
`;

const SecondChar = styled.span.attrs({ 'data-widget': 'avatar-second-char' })`
  z-index: 0;
  opacity: 0.7;
`;
```
The function `parseStyledComponents` should return the following object:
```javascript
{
  FirstChar: {
    'z-index': '1'
  },
  SecondChar: {
    'z-index': '0',
    'opacity': '0.7'
  }
}
```

### Solution:
```javascript
function parseStyledComponents(styledComponentsCode) {
  const componentProperties = {};
  const componentRegex = /const\s+(\w+)\s+=\s+styled\.\w+\s*\.\s*attrs\(([^)]+)\)`((?:[^`]|`[^$])*)`/g;
  let match;

  while ((match = componentRegex.exec(styledComponentsCode)) !== null) {
    const componentName = match[1];
    const cssProperties = match[3].match(/\s*([\w-]+)\s*:\s*([^;]+);/g);

    if (cssProperties) {
      componentProperties[componentName] = {};
      cssProperties.forEach(property => {
        const [key, value] = property.split(':').map(part => part.trim());
        componentProperties[componentName][key] = value;
      });
    }
  }

  return componentProperties;
}

// Test the function with the provided example
const styledComponentsCode = `
const FirstChar = styled.span.attrs({ singleCharacter: true })\`
  z-index: 1;
\`;

const SecondChar = styled.span.attrs({ 'data-widget': 'avatar-second-char' })\`
  z-index: 0;
  opacity: 0.7;
\`;
`;

console.log(parseStyledComponents(styledComponentsCode));
```

The `parseStyledComponents` function uses regular expressions to extract the component names and their CSS properties and values from the input styled-components code. It then constructs and returns an object containing the component names and their respective CSS properties and values.

