pub fn convert_to_rgba(pixel_data: &Vec<Vec<u32>>) -> Vec<Vec<(u8, u8, u8, u8)>> {
    pixel_data
        .iter()
        .map(|row| {
            row.iter()
                .map(|&pixel| {
                    let red = ((pixel >> 16) & 0xFF) as u8;
                    let green = ((pixel >> 8) & 0xFF) as u8;
                    let blue = (pixel & 0xFF) as u8;
                    let alpha = 255; // Set alpha channel to 255 (fully opaque)
                    (red, green, blue, alpha)
                })
                .collect()
        })
        .collect()
}
```

The `convert_to_rgba` function iterates through each row of the input pixel data and then through each pixel in the row. For each pixel, it extracts the red, green, and blue channels by bit manipulation and constructs a tuple representing the RGBA values, with the alpha channel set to 255 (fully opaque). The resulting 2D vector of tuples represents the pixel data in RGBA format.

