- `elapsed_time(&self) -> Option<Duration>`: Returns the elapsed time as a `Duration` in seconds, or `None` if the stopwatch is still running.

You should use the `std::time::Instant` to track the start and stop times of the stopwatch.

Your program should provide the following functionality:
- Create a new stopwatch.
- Start the stopwatch and record the start time.
- Stop the stopwatch and record the stop time.
- Reset the stopwatch to zero.
- Retrieve the elapsed time in seconds.

