```

Your task is to implement the necessary data structures and functions to fulfill the requirements of the library management system. You should define a `Book` struct with attributes such as `title`, `author`, and `available` to represent each book in the library. Additionally, you need to implement the following functions:

1. `add_book(title: &str, author: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>)`: This function should add a new book to the library with the given title and author.

2. `remove_book(title: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>)`: This function should remove the book with the given title from the library.

3. `search_book(title: &str, library: &Vec<Book>) -> Option<&Book>`: This function should search for a book with the given title in the library and return a reference to the book if found.

4. `check_out_book(title: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>) -> Result<(), &str>`: This function should mark the book with the given title as checked out if it's available. If the book is not available, it should return an error message.

5. `return_book(title: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>) -> Result<(), &str>`: This function should mark the book with the given title as returned if it's currently checked out. If the book is not checked out, it should return an error message.

You should use the provided `uapi` module for user interaction, which includes functions for input and output operations.

Implement the library management system according to the given requirements and code snippet.

### Solution:
```rust
use uapi::*;

struct Book {
    title: String,
    author: String,
    available: bool,
}

impl Book {
    fn new(title: &str, author: &str) -> Book {
        Book {
            title: title.to_string(),
            author: author.to_string(),
            available: true,
        }
    }
}

fn add_book(title: &str, author: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>) {
    let new_book = Book::new(title, author);
    library.push(new_book);
}

fn remove_book(title: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>) {
    library.retain(|book| book.title != title);
}

fn search_book(title: &str, library: &Vec<Book>) -> Option<&Book> {
    library.iter().find(|book| book.title == title)
}

fn check_out_book(title: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>) -> Result<(), &str> {
    if let Some(book) = library.iter_mut().find(|book| book.title == title && book.available) {
        book.available = false;
        Ok(())
    } else {
        Err("Book not available for checkout")
    }
}

fn return_book(title: &str, library: &mut Vec<Book>) -> Result<(), &str> {
    if let Some(book) = library.iter_mut().find(|book| book.title == title && !book.available) {
        book.available = true;
        Ok(())
    } else {
        Err("Book not checked out")
    }
}

fn main() {
    let mut library: Vec<Book> = Vec::new();

    add_book("The Catcher in the Rye", "J.D. Salinger", &mut library);
    add_book("To Kill a Mockingbird", "Harper Lee", &mut library);
    add_book("1984", "George Orwell", &mut library);

    let book_to_search = "To Kill a Mockingbird";
    match search_book(book_to_search, &library) {
        Some(book) => println!("Book found: {} by {}", book.title, book.author),
        None => println!("Book not found"),
    }

    let book_to_checkout = "1984";
    match check_out_book(book_to_checkout, &mut library) {
        Ok(()) => println!("{} checked out successfully", book_to_checkout),
        Err(msg) => println!("{}", msg),
    }

    let book_to_return = "1984";
    match return_book(book_to_return, &mut library) {
        Ok(()) => println!("{} returned successfully", book_to_return),
        Err(msg) => println!("{}", msg),
    }
}
```

